# Anti over-engineering

Adapted from [awesome-cursorrules anti-overengineering](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules/blob/main/rules/anti-overengineering.mdc).

- Only change what the task requires; no drive-by refactors or unrelated files.
- Prefer extending existing modules (`mbs.annotation`, `mbs.matrix`, CLI) over
  new frameworks, services, or abstraction layers.
- Follow Stage 0 order in `docs/TODO_PIPELINE.md`; do not jump to optional /
  deferred layers (ComBat, REGENIE, PROTRIDER/AE as default, ClickHouse,
  TileDB migration, etc.). Graph-layer cCRE/tiles for RBS/TBS are Milestone
  **7C**, not §8 product-surface work.
- Scaffolding, stubs, or download scripts alone do not complete a milestone.
- If a simpler approach meets acceptance criteria, use it and document the
  trade-off in `docs/plans/` or an ADR when the choice is binding.
